WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.630
- [Narrator] Adidas and Puma are two

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:03.940
of the biggest rivals in shoes.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:07.710
But did you know that their
founders were two halves

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:08.670
of a once happy.
- Hi there.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.880
- Family business.
- Hello.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.540
- [Narrator] That turned
into a level of brother rage

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:13.600
so intense
(clicking)

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.470
it will get the sneaker
heads' tongues awaggin'?

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:17.540
See what I did there?

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:22.160
In the 1930’s, the Dassler
brothers' sport shoe company

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.200
in Bavaria made the most
kick-ass athletic shoes

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.710
in all the land.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.340
The company even gave
Jesse Owens a pair of shoes

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.293
to compete in the 36th Olympics.

00:00:31.293 --> 00:00:32.592
(whistling)
When Jesse won,

00:00:32.592 --> 00:00:35.210
(cheering)
the brothers' shoes blew up.

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:38.210
But all of that success was not
good for their relationship.

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:39.570
Tensions flared.
(grunting)

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:43.170
Some say there was stealing,
affairs, resentment

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:47.270
and after World War II the
brothers were so out of step

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:48.103
they eventually
(hinge squeaks)

00:00:48.103 --> 00:00:49.050
ended the company.

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:53.600
In 1949, Adolf, or Adi Dassler,

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.470
formed Adidas a play on his nickname.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.830
Rudolf Dassler started Puma
(puma roars)

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:01.431
because, well, that name is awesome.

00:01:01.431 --> 00:01:03.460
(puma scowls)
The brothers sued each other

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:04.604
many, many times over the years

00:01:04.604 --> 00:01:05.700
(papers crinkling)

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.910
over all sorts of design
and trademark issues

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:13.290
costing each other a fortune
in lawyers and suits.

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:16.110
Their two factories built
in the same Bavarian village

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:17.520
of Herzogenaurach
(speaks in foreign language)

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.480
polarized the community with local people

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.990
picking sides by picking shoes.

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.990
The brothers died two years apart.

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:27.270
They were buried at opposite
ends of the village graveyard.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:28.760
Proof that even in death
(thunder claps)

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:32.030
there remained a great
bitter divide between them.

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:36.060
And so it was for decades until 2009.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.870
Employees of Adidas
and Puma in the village

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:39.998
where the two companies still

00:01:39.998 --> 00:01:41.140
(cheering)
have their headquarters

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:44.330
came together and played
a friendly soccer match.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:47.870
And started the process of
healing decades of enmity.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:51.800
And began a new era of love and shoes.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:54.967
(quirky upbeat music)

00:01:57.261 --> 00:01:59.928
(tonal ringing)

